 "notes": "Start: p.222 line '1.' àn; end: p.224 line 10 ḥeḥ en sep above the short rule; Appendix (with its own footnote, Naville Bd. I., Bl. 140) excluded. Rubric: p.222 row 1 overline covers àn and unχ-f..θàb only (Àusàr, Ani, maāχeru not overlined); rows 2-3 fully overlined. p.223 rows 1-4 fully overlined; row 5 overlined from Rā to en (after àb), not over suten, again over final em; row 6 (śeni-f .. en) not overlined. p.224: no overlines. Numerals 2. (inside tebtu) and 9. (inside setau - tuf) fall mid-word; those words kept on the preceding line. Glosses: the English is continuous so alignment is approximate; en on p.223 line 5 has no separate English. Recurring uncertain glyphs: seated figure with raised arm (A1 coded), seated long-wigged figure (B1 coded, may be A40), round handled jar (W1 coded), bucket pot (W10 approx), small cone (M44 approx). The thin dashed vertical after words coded Z1."
